                            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived stack
                  %h2#theorems Theorems
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barr%27s+theorem"} Barr's theorem
                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/topos+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#RelationToSieves"} Relation to sieves
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_simplicial_presheaves"} Relation to simplicial presheaves
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            %em local epimorphism
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            over the site which becomes an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
          %p
            More abstractly, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %em local epimorphisms
            is a system of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, Set]
            that has the closure properties expected of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            and under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
          %p
            There is then a unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            that induces this system of local epimorphism, see
            %em
              %a{:href => "#RelationToSieves"} Relation to sieves
            below.
          %p
            Moreover the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphisms"} local isomorphisms
            among the local epimorphisms admit a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
            which equips the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            with the structure of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            on the site
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
          %h2#definition Definition
          #SystemOfLocalEpimorphisms.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (system of local epimorphisms)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %em system of local epimorphisms
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{S}^{op}, Set]
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              satisfying the following axioms:
            %p
              %strong LE1
              every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{S}^{op}, Set]
              is a local epimorphism;
            %p
              %strong LE2
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composite
              of two local epimorphisms is a local epimorphism;
            %p
              %strong LE3
              if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi u
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi v
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1 \stackrel{u}{\to} A_2 \stackrel{v}{\to} A_3
              is a local epimorphism, then so is
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            %p
              %strong LE4
              a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \colon A \to B
              is a local epimorphism precisely if for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in \mathcal{S}
              (regarded as a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+presheaf"} representable presheaf
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y: U \to B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times_B U \to U
              is a local epimorphism.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToSieves Relation to sieves
          %p
            The specification of a system of local epimorphisms is equivalent to a system of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck covering
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieves"} sieves
          %p To see this, translate between local epimorphisms to sieves as follows.
          %p
            Throughout, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{S}^{op}, Set]
            for its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            and write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  y \;\colon\; \mathcal{S} \longrightarrow [\mathcal{S}^{op}, Set]
          %p
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
          #LocalEpimorphismFromGrothendieckTopology.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (local epimorphisms from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            %p
              Let the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              be equipped with a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in \mathcal{S}
              an object in the site, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
              into the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+presheaf"} represented presheaf
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} y(U)
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\in [\mathcal{S}^{op}, Set]
            %p
              is a
              %em local epimorphism
              if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sieve
                      %mi A
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sieve_A \subset y(U) \in [S^{op}, Set]
            %p
              at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              which assigns to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              all morphisms from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              that factor through
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sieve
                      %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi V
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi V
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi g
                      %mi U
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mo ∃
                              %mo ↗
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↓
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mi f
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi V
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %mi y
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi U
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sieve_f
                    \\;\colon\;
                    V
                    \\;\mapsto\;
                    \\left\{  V \overset{g}{\to} U \,\in \mathcal{S}
                    \\;\Big\vert\;
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\exists}}\nearrow &amp; \Big\downarrow{}^{f}
                    \\\
                    y(V) &amp; \underset{y(g)}{\longrightarrow} &amp; y(U)
                    }
                    \\right\}
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+sieve"} covering sieve
            %p A general morphism of presheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \overset{}{\longrightarrow} B \;\;\; \in [\mathcal{S}^{op}, Set]
            %p
              is a
              %em local epimorphism
              if for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in \mathcal{S}
              and every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(U) \to B
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
              morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(U) \times_{B} A \overset{p_1}{\to} y(V)
              out of the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi B
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi pb
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↓
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    y(U)\times_{B} A
                    \&amp;\overset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    A
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{p_1}}\Big\downarrow
                    \&amp;{}^{(pb)}&amp; \Big\downarrow{}^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    y(U) &amp;\underset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B
                    }
            %p
              is a local epimorphism as above. By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sieve
                      %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi V
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi V
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi g
                      %mi U
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi V
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
